    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process there is one black triangle. Find a formula for the number of black triangles after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3^n$",
          "worked": "Each black triangle becomes three black triangles at the next iteration. The number forms a geometric sequence with first term 1 at iteration 0 and common ratio 3.\n$$N_n=1\\times3^n=3^n.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process there are zero removed triangles. Find a formula for the number of removed triangles after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3^n-1}{2}$\n\nSum the numbers removed at successive iterations: $1,3,9,\\ldots$.",
          "worked": "At iteration $k$, one triangle is removed from each of the $3^{k-1}$ black triangles. Thus, for $n\\geq1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}R_n&=1+3+3^2+\\cdots+3^{n-1}\\\\R_n&=\\frac{3^n-1}{3-1}\\\\R_n&=\\frac{3^n-1}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe formula also gives $R_0=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process the total area that remains is $\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{4}$. Find a formula for the total area that remains after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\left(\\dfrac34\\right)^n$",
          "worked": "Each iteration retains three of the four congruent triangles, so the remaining area is multiplied by $\\frac34$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A_n&=A_0\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n\\\\A_n&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "After 0 iterations of the above process the total area that has been removed is zero. Find a formula for the total area that has been removed after $n$ iterations.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\left[1-\\left(\\dfrac34\\right)^n\\right]$",
          "worked": "The removed area is the original area minus the remaining area.\n$$\\begin{align*}D_n&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n\\\\D_n&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\left[1-\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n\\right].\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q23-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find the area of Sierpinski’s triangle.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$.\n\nThe remaining area tends to zero because $0<\\frac34<1$.",
          "worked": "Since $0<\\frac34<1$, the powers $\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n$ tend to zero.\n$$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}A_n=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}\\left(\\frac34\\right)^n=0.$$\nSierpinski’s triangle has area 0.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
